\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen hits 4-month high vs dollar.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn   \par \uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The yen hit four-month highs against the dollar on Thursday as markets tested the Japanese monetary authorities' resolve to cap its strength ahead of a meeting of Group of Seven industrialised nations this weekend.   \par \par \uc2 Markets are wary of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to protect their country's fragile export-led recovery after record levels of official yen sales this year.   \par \par \uc2 But they are also wary that the United States will chastise \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at the G7 meeting in Dubai, and that if Japan stands away from the market, the yen will rally sharply.   \par \par \uc2 "Markets are questioning what is going on with the MOF," said Steven Saywell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank, referring to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The risk of the authorities moving aside is low, but capital flows are positive for Japan, so they are going to have a battle on their hands."   \par \par \uc2 The yen rose by a third of a percent from the U.S. close to 115.68 by 0725 GMT, its strongest showing since May. Japanese stocks ended at a 15-month high on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Non-Japanese fund operators were rumoured to be selling dollars in an effort to trigger inflating option sell orders placed at 115.50 and 115.00 yen, Tokyo dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The yen gained on the euro to 130.56, within recent ranges.   \par \par \uc2 The yen was gaining from growing speculation that overseas hedge funds would increase their exposure to Japanese stocks, Tokyo dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Financial sources said several major European and U.S. hedge funds were in Tokyo this week meeting politicians and influential analysts, seeking information about the next Japanese administration in order to decide on potential investments.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is confident in buying the yen as pressure mounts on Asia, but if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anyway this bet will prove wrong and a nasty squeeze will follow," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.   \par \par \uc2 EURO OUTLOOK   \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Thursday, but is not expected to discuss monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.1275, slightly below the New York close but near the top of recent ranges, after breaking through key technical levels in the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 The IMF said in its World Economic Outlook on Thursday that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to cut rates again if the euro goes up significantly and that Japan's economy was still vulnerable.   \par \par \uc2 Its chief economist, Kenneth Rogoff, also said the U.S. current account deficit must some day unwind, causing a sharp fall in the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The Swiss National Bank issues its quarterly monetary policy review around 1200 GMT, and is widely expected to maintain the generous stance that has kept short-term Swiss rates near zero.   \par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc was steady against the euro at 1.5567, compared with three-year lows of 1.5625 set on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc was also steady against the dollar at 1.3792, close to its lowest levels since mid-August.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. weekly jobless claims at 1230 GMT are expected to come in at 410,000, from the previous 422,000.   \par \par \uc2 The September Philadelphia Fed survey, due at 1600 GMT, is forecast to weaken to a reading of 17.3, from the previous 22.1.   \par \par \uc2 Sterling hit one-month highs against the dollar of $1.6123 on Thursday, extending gains made after minutes of the Bank of England's latest monetary meeting released on Wednesday fuelled talk of a UK rate rise.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030918dz9i001cr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
