\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slips Vs Yen, But 116 Holds On MOF Talk \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2003\par 07:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar slipped against the yen in Asia Wednesday, as market participants stayed on high alert for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but warily tested the downside ahead of a Group of Seven meeting. \par \par \uc2  The perception that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell yen to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising helped keep the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above key support at Y116. \par \par \uc2  But some market participants tested the downside on the premise that the MOF might hesitate to raise the ire of its G7 partners by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen strength before this weekend's G7 finance ministers' and central bankers' meeting in Dubai. \par \par \uc2  The question of the day was whether Japanese banks' morning dollar buys just above Y116 were covert Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on MOF's behalf, or whether activity was done on behalf of holders of options with that strike. \par \par \uc2  "It's impossible" to say for sure which it was, said a U.S. brokerage trader, adding that perhaps "there was even a little of both." MOF must know about massive stop loss orders said to lie just below Y116 and might be covertly defending that level, he said. \par \par \uc2  Most believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will come up at this weekend's G7 meeting, but strategists and market participants had mixed opinions on what would emerge from the talks. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. knows Japan's economic recovery "is important for the global economy as a whole," said Credit Suisse First Boston strategist Satoru Ogasawara. As the U.S. is now asking Japan to contribute to the Iraq rebuilding effort, "they can't complain too much about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have much room to contribute, with the budget deficit so high," and any economic setback would further weigh on any contribution, he said. \par \par \uc2  The market virtually ignored the U.S. Federal Reserve's widely expected decision overnight to leave benchmark rates on hold at a 45-year low of 1%. The policy-setting Federal Open Market Committee said rates will remain low for a "considerable period." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.09, below Y116.18 in New York and Y117.06 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1148, lower than $1.1169 in New York and $1.1303 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y129.42, compared with Y129.80 in New York and Y132.36 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5874, compared with $1.5866 in New York and $1.6043 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Even market participants selling dollars know that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry is notorious for holding its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fire until massive short-dollar positions build, prompting a wave of short-covering. \par \par \uc2  The ministry apparently held off selling yen for a while during the Tokyo visit of U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, a vocal critic of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But on Sept. 4, after the dollar fell to Y115.76, the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively on the ministry's behalf, pushing the dollar up more than a yen. \par \par \uc2  Therefore, market conditions rather than the looming G7 meeting are more key to the timing of any yen-selling by Japanese authorities, many market participants and observers say. \par \par \uc2  "Looking at the MOF's past performance, we see no indication that G7 meetings have proved any obstacle to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Deutsche Bank strategist Marshall Gittler, citing MOF's Y3.9 trillion selling spree over the 10-day span around the May G8 finance ministers' meeting. \par \par \uc2  "We look for another bear trap like that which caught so many people following Snow's visit," Gittler said. "We would prefer to be long dollar/yen at these levels." \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, too, the yen remained buoyant. \par \par \uc2  Although Japanese exporters sold the euro over the past seven sessions when it hit highs above Y130, some continued to sell into rises Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In addition to exporter selling, Japanese investors' continued to unwind hedges on eurozone investments made earlier this year, and European investors still sought yen to invest in Japanese equities. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Bennett Richardson \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030917dz9h00097\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shp