\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar retreats on profit-taking - low rates weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2003\par 19:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 17 (Reuters)-The dollar weakened against European counterparts on Wednesday on profit-taking from Tuesday's gains, with investors concerned about low U.S. interest rates, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 But the greenback rose against the yen, with traders attributing the dollar's advance to profit-taking on the Japanese unit following its steep recent gains, rather than Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "What we're seeing is a reversal of the dollar's gains after the FOMC meeting and the rally in stocks yesterday," said Ronald Simpson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS in New York. "The market is pretty much in a range-trading mentality."  \par \par \uc2 The euro was up 0.52 percent on the day at $1.1234 .  \par \par \uc2 Brian Taylor, head \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Manufacturers and Traders Bank in Buffalo, New York, said the market had been "overextended" in the euro going into Wednesday's session and had seized on some good buying opportunities at the $1.1150-$1.1175 area.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the greenback fell 0.49 percent to 1.3826 francs . Sterling gained a sharp 1.07 percent against the dollar at $1.6045 after minutes from the Bank of England's rate meeting in early September showed some policy-makers starting to look for an interest rate rise.  \par \par \uc2 Gains in sterling versus the dollar have also helped boost other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the greenback, specifically the euro, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 LOW-RATE BURDEN  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the dollar also reeled from the after-effects of a Federal Reserve policy meeting that kept interest rates at a 45-year low and cautioned against softness in the labor market and the lingering threat of disinflation.  \par \par \uc2 "What has partly hurt the dollar is the fact that the Fed indicated an accommodative policy stance for a sustained period," said John McCarthy, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Capital Markets in New York.  \par \par \uc2 With rates expected to remain at troughs for some time, analysts said investors have temporarily disregarded the U.S. economic rebound story and started looking once again at high-yielders such as the Australian dollar, New Zealand dollar and Canadian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 MMS' Simpson reckons that since the U.S. economy may be fast running out of positive surprises and the soft labor sector continues to weigh on the market, the dollar's upside may be limited until the end of September.  \par \par \uc2 G7 MEETING  \par \par \uc2 Ahead of the Group of Seven meeting this weekend in Dubai, the yen is a major focus in the market as investors puzzle over whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undertaking yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials said they would act on foreign exchanges if they saw a need, delivering a fresh warning to prevent any tendency in the yen to appreciate - even though this policy may meet criticism from U.S. officials at the G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.23 percent against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 115.88 yen . The euro climbed against the yen, up 0.28 percent at 130.21 yen .  \par \par \uc2 Increasingly, more and more traders were saying that the BoJ was not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the yen weaker against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Taylor, of Manufacturers and Traders Bank, believes the BoJ's hands are tied ahead of the G7 and expects further yen strengthening. "Once we get through 115 yen, there's not much the BoJ can do below that level," he said.  \par \par \uc2 ING's McCarthy also said the BoJ cannot risk taking the heat for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prior to the G7 gathering.  \par \par \uc2 The BoJ, which acts on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was unavailable for comment.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect yen sentiment to swing ahead of the meeting between equities optimism - after Wednesday's 15-month closing high in the Nikkei stock average - to wariness over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Additional reporting by Burton Frierson in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030917dz9h002uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
