\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Volatilities Surge Along With Spot Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2003\par 18:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Volatilities implied by one-month dollar/yen and euro/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options rose sharply Tuesday in New York, as the yen jumped to one-week highs against its major counterparts in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Speculators bought heavily into the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an apparent bid to test the resolve of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of this weekend's G7 meeting. Finance ministers in the U.S. and Europe are expected to pressure Japan to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move more freely, though China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg is the bigger focus. \par \par \uc2  However, it appears that the BOJ, working on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may be keeping the dollar from falling below Y116.20, with a senior dealer at a Japanese bank in New York saying that the "same old persistent buyer" was rumored to be on bid at that level. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very nervous on the downside for dollar/yen, and there are lots of barriers," said Terry Li, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives specialist at HSBC Bank, adding that a break through those barriers could trigger more stop-losses and push the dollar to Y115. \par \par \uc2  He sees volatilities rising to 9.5%-10.0% on a spot-market move down to Y115.75 and to 10.5%-11.0% if it falls below Y115. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, euro/dollar volatilities are largely unchanged because the market "thinks the euro is in a range between $1.1150 and $1.13," said Li, adding that a move below that range would likely push up volatilities. \par \par \uc2  Late morning Tuesday in New York, the dollar was at Y116.25, down from Y117.50 late Monday in New York. The euro was trading around $1.1187, down from $1.1283 Monday. It was also at Y130.05, from Y132.56. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options implied volatility of 8.8%-9.1%, up from 7.85%-8.15% earlier in Tokyo and 7.80%-8.10% in New York Monday. \par \par \uc2  One-month euro/dollar option volatilities were at 10.5%-10.8%, little changed from 10.5%-10.7% in Tokyo and 10.6%/10.8% in New York Monday. \par \par \uc2  One-month euro/yen option volatilities were at 11.3%-11.6%, up from 10.80%-11.15% earlier in Tokyo and in New York Monday. \par \par \uc2  One-month risk-reversals on dollar/yen favor yen calls at 1.4% to 1.8%, up from 1.05% to 1.35% Monday in New York. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  Euro calls were favored by 0.1% to 0.5%, down from 0.3% to 0.7% Monday. \par \par \uc2  Volatility measures the expected range in the value of an asset over the period of the contract. Volatilities on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options gauge the anticipated moves in the underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a higher volatility implying a wider trading range. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Barkley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385; tom.barkley@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 44427 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030916dz9g0013l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
