\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up amid broad yen gains, shrugs off Fed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kyle Peterson  \par \uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2003\par 22:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The dollar soared against its European rivals on Tuesday, indirectly lifted by the rallying yen as investors ignored a Federal Reserve decision to leave interest rates steady.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback gained about 1 percent against the euro but lost at least that much against the yen after the benchmark Nikkei stock index turned in a strong performance overnight and the Bank of Japan raised its view on the world's second-largest economy in its monthly report.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's sharp gains, particularly against the euro, commanded more market attention than the Fed's policy-setting committee. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its overnight lending rate at a 45-year low of 1 percent, but warned of a risk that inflation could become "undesirably low."  \par \par \uc2 "Everybody had really priced in what happened," said Lara Rhame, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "The implication are that rates are going to remain very, very low for some time," she said. "I think that is going to imply some dollar weakness, particularly against the euro, going forward."  \par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday, the dollar drew support from the sharp rally in the yen, which weighed heavily on European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro fell 2 percent against the yen and 1 percent against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In late New York trading, the euro was down 0.95 percent on the day at $1.1177 . Against the Swiss franc, the greenback was up 0.7 percent to 1.3896 francs . Sterling was down 0.8 percent against the dollar at $1.5875 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar declined 1.12 percent against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 116.10 yen . The euro fell steeply against the yen, down 2.11 percent at 129.75 yen .  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar is being helped by the yen's rise across the board," said Steven Englander, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for North America at Barclay's Capital.  \par \par \uc2 "When the yen strengthens across the board, the euro normally weakens against the dollar," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the yen's rising influence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is being driven by expectations that Japan will be one of the biggest winners in a global economic recovery. Given its huge trade surplus with most countries, Japan is well-positioned to benefit from a global upswing in the industrial production cycle.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were also speculating \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may hold off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen gains ahead of a Group of Seven ministerial meeting this weekend. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a key issue during the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. CONSUMER PRICE DATA  \par \par \uc2 Weaker-than-expected consumer price numbers for August hardly made a dent on the dollar's overall performance. August CPI data showed an increase of 0.3 percent, slightly lower than market expectations of a 0.4 percent rise.  \par \par \uc2 But excluding food and energy costs, the "core" CPI was up 0.1 percent last month, compared with a rise of 0.2 percent in July.  \par \par \uc2 "For the United States, the disinflationary trend continues," said Sal Guateri, senior economist at BMO Financial Group in Toronto. "This portrays an economy operating with a lot of slack, i.e., unused capacity. For the dollar, it is a near-term negative because the Fed will keep rates low for a long time," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030917dz9g0018w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
