\par\par \b \uc2 Japan seen defending yen policy at G7 meeting.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tamawa Kadoya  \par \uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2003\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Japan will be happy to see its Group of Seven partners echoing its call for China to adopt a flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime at a meeting this week but will refuse to budge on its own policy of beating down the buoyant yen.   \par \par \uc2  Illness has forced Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa - a vocal critic of a virtually pegged Chinese yuan and what he calls speculative forces trying to push up the yen - to miss the G7 meeting in Dubai, but deputy Zembei Mizoguchi and Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui will pick up where he left off.   \par \par \uc2  High on the agenda will be the yuan's de facto peg to the dollar, which critics say gives China an unfair trade advantage by keeping its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervalued, but similar charges could be levelled at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in record amounts this year to rein in the yen.   \par \par \uc2  "The communique is unlikely to point out Japan's policy specifically, but markets expect that the general tone at the meeting will be some kind of pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at JP Morgan Chase in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2  Tokyo spent around nine trillion yen ($77 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first eight months of the year and was thought to be in the market this month to prevent the dollar tumbling towards 115 yen, seen as a key line of defence.   \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the dollar traded at around 116.50 yen.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month Canadian Finance Minister John Manley said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a topic at the Dubai meeting, a sign of discontent among at least some of the G7 partners over Japan's unilateral market action.   \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the G7 - the United States, Japan, Germany, Britain, France, Italy and Canada - meet in Dubai at the weekend on the fringes of the semi-annual meetings of the World Bank and International Monetary Fund.   \par \par \uc2  EXPORT-LED RECOVERY   \par \par \uc2  From \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's point of view, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed merely at stemming what it deems an excessive rise in the yen so as to keep its export-led recovery intact.   \par \par \uc2  "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should basically be decided by markets," Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi told reporters on Tuesday, adding that too much fluctuation was undesirable.   \par \par \uc2  Koizumi also said any decision on the yuan was for China to make, not Japan.   \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, echoed Koizumi's view on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.   \par \par \uc2  "We are not trying to lead the markets in any one direction," he told reporters.   \par \par \uc2  To a certain extent, the Japanese authorities' renewed forays into the market this month, after they stayed out in August, have reinforced the view that they had the tacit approval of Washington and others to keep selling yen.   \par \par \uc2  "The fact that Tokyo is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  means that the U.S. is acknowledging its actions," said Eisuke Sakakibara, one of Mizoguchi's predecessors, who earned the monicker "Mr Yen" for his influence on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.   \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. administration's stance is that they will not allow \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the yen further down, but will tolerate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yen's rise," he added. "I don't think that will change" after the G7 meeting.   \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, mindful that Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi was battling for re-election as ruling party chief on September 20 against a field of anti-reform rivals, was careful not to directly criticise Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy when he visited Tokyo earlier this month.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Washington has avoided overtly criticising Tokyo not only because it recognises its economic problems, but also because it wants its support in a larger political context.   \par \par \uc2  "What the U.S. seeks most strongly is for Japan to share the burden in rebuilding Iraq and Afghanistan. There is the North Korea issue as well. They don't want to aggravate the U.S.-Japan relationship over \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Takatoshi Kato, a former vice finance minister for international affairs who is now an adviser at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.   \par \par \uc2  But Snow said last week that he would stress the importance of flexible exchange rates at the G7 meeting.   \par \par \uc2  In addition, with Japan's economy on the mend - it logged 3.9 percent real annualised growth in the April-June quarter - its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy may be harder to defend.   \par \par \uc2  Europe's top financial officials said on Saturday that Asia's weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were causing problems for the euro and urged China and Japan to share the pain of unwinding the enormous U.S. current account deficit. ($1=117.40 Yen) (Additional reporting by Ritsuko Shimizu).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030916dz9g00272\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
