\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slides as yen gains gather pace.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Charlotte Cooper  \par \uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2003\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The dollar fell more than three quarters of a percent against the yen on Tuesday as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rode the back of a strong close on Tokyo stock markets and traders tested Bank of Japan resolve to curb its gains.  \par \par \uc2 The yen climbed more than one percent on the euro as well after the TOPIX index closed 1.86 percent up at a 15-month high, driven largely by bank stocks.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said there was some speculation Japanese authorities may hold off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen gains ahead of a Group of Seven (G7) ministerial meeting in Dubai this weekend in order to deflect criticism over yen policy from other nations.  \par \par \uc2 "There is continued dollar weakness. Also markets may be picking up on some hesitation to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of G7," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London.  \par \par \uc2 "There is also improving economic data, the Bank of Japan upgraded its economic outlook, an ongoing shift into Japanese stocks and more foreign inflows into the yen."  \par \par \uc2 By 0825 GMT the yen had gained 0.75 percent to 116.53 per dollar and 1.15 percent to 131.03 yen, nearly two yen up from a near four-week low set on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was 0.3 percent lower on the day at $1.1265 and half a cent off a four-week peak set on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The market is also waiting for a Federal Reserve interest rate decision at 1815 GMT on Tuesday. Forecasts are for no change in rates but the market will scrutinise any Fed assessment of the economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 SNOWBALL'S CHANCE  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspect Japanese authorities have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past week or so to keep the dollar supported against the yen in order to prevent a rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  damaging an export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials reiterated their intention to curb yen strengthen. Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Tuesday that any action Japan takes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is aimed at preventing volatility and overshooting.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi also shrugged off speculation that other G7 countries may urge \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at their weekend summit, saying he saw no need to explain Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position further at the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts in London said there was speculation in the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hold off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the meeting to deflect criticism about its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy from G7 partners.  \par \par \uc2 But Derek Halpenny, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to let dollar/yen fall far ahead of a leadership election in Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's ruling LDP party this Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 "You can have 'hands off' for another big figure - I can't rule that out," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "But the big picture policy agenda is protecting 115 (on dollar/yen) and there is not a snowball's chance in hell of that being let go ahead of the LDP presidential elections at the weekend."  \par \par \uc2 Koizumi is expected to be re-elected as party president, ensuring he keeps the nation's top job.  \par \par \uc2 He is then expected to reshuffle his cabinet and there is some speculation that he may replace Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, 81, who is not going to next weekend's G7 meeting after suffering from gall bladder inflammation.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. RECOVERY?  \par \par \uc2 Mixed U.S. data has halted the dollar's recent rally from a record low against the euro in June, with weaker than expected industrial output data on Monday adding to the view the economy may not rebound as strongly as markets had been expecting.  \par \par \uc2 August consumer prices data is due at 1230 GMT and is forecast to show a rise of 0.4 percent compared with a 0.2 percent increase in July.  \par \par \uc2 In Europe, Germany's ZEW September index of economic sentiment, viewed as a useful precursor to the IFO business sentiment index, is due at 0900 GMT. It is forecast to rise to 59.0 from 52.5.  \par \par \uc2 The euro touched its highest level in three years against the Swiss franc at 1.5625 francs. Markets are waiting to see what the Swiss National Bank will say in its quarterly review on Thursday. Finance Minister Kaspar Villiger said he would step down at the end of this legislation.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030916dz9g0024m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
