\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan MOF official says G7 to discuss  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2003\par 08:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Group of Seven ministers will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when they meet in Dubai this week, a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The official, speaking to reporters on condition of anonymity, declined to say whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be brought up but said he did not expect the views of the G7 nations on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  to deviate from past statements.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm sure there will be discussions on how \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should be," he said. "But I don't think their respective views will be that different from what has been said."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in record amounts this year to keep the yen down to help reflate the economy. Tokyo has so far officially spent about nine trillion yen ($76.7 billion), exceeding the previous high of 7.6 trillion in 1999.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have repeatedly said that excessive movements are undesirable and that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reflect fundamentals and move stably.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 nations agree they should closely monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and cooperate as needed, a standard phrase used in recent G7 communiques.  \par \par \uc2 "Sometimes there are excesssive fluctuations and it is necessary to discuss how to handle such movements," the official said.  \par \par \uc2 Asked whether China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy would be discussed, the official said discussions were progressing on the issue and that talks at the G7 meeting would likely to be along that line.  \par \par \uc2 The United States and European nations have recently joined calls by Japan for China to loosen its de facto peg to the dollar, which many say keeps the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervalued.  \par \par \uc2 On the global economy, the official said a recovery was occurring faster than had been expected and that downside risks had largely receded.  \par \par \uc2 Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the G7 - the United States, Britain, Japan, Germany, France, Italy and Canada - are set to meet in Dubai on the fringes of the semi-annual meetings of the World Bank and International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Tuesday that he would not attend due to recent illness.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's delegation will be headed by Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui and Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi. ($1=117.40 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030916dz9g001qv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
