\par\par \b \uc2 Dlr holds above Y117 on wariness BOJ will  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chikafumi Hodo  \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2003\par 05:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 12 (Reuters) - The dollar was trapped in tight ranges on Friday, but it was firmly protected near 117 yen due to wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of stepping in during New York trade.  \par \par \uc2 Traders cited unnatural and persistent bids after the dollar rapidly fell to a New York low of 116.45 yen on weak U.S. jobs data, drawing strong speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen.  \par \par \uc2 "After seeing the dollar was firmly protected, (Tokyo) players have become cautious about holding on to their short positions ahead of the three-day weekend," said Yukihiro Shimoyamada, a vice president at UFJ Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the dollar is on a slight upward trend, with the possibility of it testing 118 yen in the near term."  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial markets will be closed on Monday for a national holiday - Respect for the Aged.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese monetary authorities were seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times this week, after the yen's upswing picked up pace as upbeat Japanese stocks and bullish economic indicators encouraged active yen-buying, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Friday that a further rise in the yen was unwarranted despite an improving economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 At 0321 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 117.07/12 yen almost identical to Thursday's late U.S. level of 117.08/16.  \par \par \uc2 RETAIL SALES IN FOCUS  \par \par \uc2 The dollar may have been solidly protected around 117 yen, but the market had placed strong sell orders above 117.50 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Yen-buying interest in the cross market also indirectly weighed on the dollar/yen rate, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Investors, who have suffered from heavy losses in Japanese government bonds (JGBs), were eagerly collecting profits from euro-denominated bond investments to cover the losses ahead of half-year book closings at the end of September, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters also showed strong inclination to sell euros above 131 yen, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 131.05/10 yen compared with 131.22/34.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback regained some strength against the euro, with market bears covering shorts as tensions receded over the possibility of a serious incident on the second anniversary of the September 11 attacks.  \par \par \uc2 The euro stood at $1.1191/95 against Thursday's $1.1201/07.  \par \par \uc2 Still, weak U.S. jobs data released on Thursday prevented market players from expanding dollar positions heavily.  \par \par \uc2 Weekly jobless claims climbed to 422,000 last week. Analysts had expected a dip to 400,000 after the previous week's surprise jump to a revised 419,000.  \par \par \uc2 The market's focus has turned to U.S. retail sales data later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 "There are still plenty of reasons to sell the dollar, given renewed uncertainty about the U.S. economic outlook since last week's jobs data and persistent tensions in the Middle East," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the corporate desk at Trust and Custody Services Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "It will be very important to see today's retail sales data to judge the outlook for the economy."  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters estimated that retail sales rose 1.4 percent in August after a 1.4 percent gain in July. Excluding automobiles, they predicted retail sales rose 0.8 percent, also the same as July.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030912dz9c000s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
