\par\par \b \uc2 Dlr boxed in as BOJ wariness dominates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2003\par 03:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 12 (Reuters) - The dollar was trapped in tight ranges on Friday, but it was firmly protected near 117 yen due to wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of stepping in during New York trade.  \par \par \uc2 Traders cited unnatural and persistent bids after the dollar rapidly fell to a New York low of 116.45 yen on weak U.S. jobs data, drawing strong speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen.  \par \par \uc2 "After seeing the dollar was firmly protected, (Tokyo) players have become cautious about holding on to their short positions ahead of the three-day weekend," said Yukihiro Shimoyamada, a vice president at UFJ Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the dollar is on a slight upward trend, with the possibility of it testing 118 yen in the near term."  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial markets will be closed on Monday for a national holiday - Respect for the Aged.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese monetary authorities were seen interening several times this week, after the yen's upswing picked up pace as upbeat Japanese stocks and bullish economic indicators encouraged active yen-buying, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Friday that a further rise in the yen was unwarranted despite an improving economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi told reporters that the government was keeping an eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that excessive moves were inappropriate.  \par \par \uc2 At 0116 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 117.20/25 yen compared with Thursday's late U.S. level of 117.08/16.  \par \par \uc2 Commercial dollar demand ahead of the long weekend also provided support at 117 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar regained some strength against the euro, with market bears covering shorts as tensions receded over the possibility of a serious incident on the second anniversary of the September 11 attacks.  \par \par \uc2 But weak U.S. jobs data prevented market players from expanding dollar positions heavily.  \par \par \uc2 Weekly jobless claims climbed to 422,000 last week. Analysts had expected a dip to 400,000 after the previous week's surprise jump to a revised 419,000.  \par \par \uc2 The market's focus has turned to U.S. retail sales data later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 The euro stood at $1.1185/90 against Thursday's $1.1201/07.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 131.11/16 yen compared with 131.22/34.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was facing constant selling from Japanese exporters eager to lock in their euro proceeds ahead of interim fiscal book closings at the end of September, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030912dz9c0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
