\par\par \b \uc2 Yen strength proves key to euro weakness vs dollar.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2003\par 22:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 11 (Reuters) - A main catalyst for the euro's slip against the dollar on Thursday was the resurgent yen's pressure on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's economic recovery is becoming a dominant theme in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, bolstered by surprisingly robust gross domestic product data from Japan on Wednesday. A brighter economic outlook in Japan is lifting the yen, which is being only restrained by the persistent threat of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts.   \par \par \uc2  By late afternoon on Thursday in New York, the euro was weaker against the yen, down 0.11 percent at 131.09 yen . The euro fell 0.06 percent against the dollar to $1.1202 , even as the labor market situation in the United States continued to languish.   \par \par \uc2  "The yen is the big focus of the market right now," said Kenneth Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in New York.   \par \par \uc2  Investors are expressing Japan's positive economic outlook through trades in the euro against the yen instead of dollar/yen transactions, according to Philip Capone, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Fortis Bank in New York.   \par \par \uc2  "It's no secret that the yen is the biggest reflation trade. It is the liquid proxy for Asia," said Capone.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Japan, more than the United States, is well positioned to benefit from a global upswing in the industrial production cycle given its huge trade surplus with most countries.   \par \par \uc2  The U.S. has a hefty current account deficit - a broad measure of the nation's global trade and which stands around 5 percent of gross domestic product - and this gives traders an incentive to push the dollar down against the yen.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOCUS ON DOLLAR/YEN   \par \par \uc2  But because the bulk of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been undertaken via dollar purchases, that has dissuaded the market from pushing the yen up much against the greenback.   \par \par \uc2  By contrast, euro-yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BoJ has been paltry in 2003, estimated at only about 2 percent of total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds employed, according to Deutsche Bank research.   \par \par \uc2  Michael Cairns, trading manager at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Solutions in New Jersey, said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's performance against the yen is a poor indicator of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth prospects because of persistent Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Without BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar would be at 112 yen, said Capone of Fortis Bank.   \par \par \uc2  In the case of dollar purchases against the yen, the BoJ, which acts on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , periodically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling yen and buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a move to protect its exporters' competitive advantage in the global marketplace.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities are believed to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently since the start of the week, displeased with the dollar's fall to near four-month lows last week below 116.0 yen.   \par \par \uc2  But with respect to the euro-yen pair, analysts say the BoJ hardly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although there is growing evidence that there could be more Japanese government action in the future. About two weeks ago, the Japanese Finance Ministry had warned the markets about the rapid move in the euro/yen, according to a Deutsche Bank note. (Daniel Bases in New York contributed to this report).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030911dz9b006fo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
