\par\par \b \uc2  Tsy's Snow:Flexible Exchange Rates To Be On Dubai Agenda \b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2003\par 21:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON -(Dow Jones)- Argentina's latest economic reform agreement with the International Monetary Fund contains "significant" structural reform requirements, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "With strong implementation by Argentina of the program's macroeconomic framework and reform measures, and with a good faith effort to reach prompt agreement on a comprehensive debt restructuring, the program can help Argentina lay the basis for sustained growth and rising living standards," Snow told reporters in a press conference ahead of his visit to the Middle East next week. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, IMF Managing Director Horst Koehler said he would recommend the Fund's executive board approve a $12.5 billion, three-year credit program once the government clears repayment arrears. Although the IMF had earlier argued Argentina needed to raise utility rates to ensure adequate power supplies going forward, and for a comprehensive plan to recapitalize the banking system, Argentine President Nestor Kirchner said the deal contains neither requirement. \par \par \uc2  The centerpiece of the deal appears to be a requirement for a primary budget surplus of at least 3% of gross domestic product in 2004, with budget targets for 2005 and 2006 left for future negotiation. \par \par \uc2  However, Snow, without specifying, said Argentina had promised "significant structural reform in this agreement dealing with utilities, the banking sector, the primary surplus and so on." \par \par \uc2  "I commend both the IMF and Argentina for being able to reach this agreement," Snow said. The Treasury Secretary said he was "very pleased" with the agreement. \par \par \uc2  He dismissed the suggestion the U.S. changed tack in the negotiations with Argentina, first stressing the need for tough reform and later pushing for those demands to be dropped. "I don't know that properly characterizes what happened," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The political leadership of Argentina has made a serious commitment to us and the IMF they will reach those targets of 3%-plus primary surplus, plus deal with the issue of an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Snow said. The Kirchner government also pledged to withdraw provincial powers to issue debt and create money, he said. \par \par \uc2  The government has pledged "meaningful improvements" in both the utility sector and the banking sector, Snow said. \par \par \uc2  Snow will travel next week to the Middle East for 10 days of talks with officials in five countries. He will wrap up the visit by attending the joint IMF-World Bank annual meetings in Dubai. At a Group of Eight leading nations meeting of finance ministers that will precede the broader meetings of finance officials, Snow said he plans to stress the importance of flexible exchange rates for all countries. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said he would repeat his view that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a minimum, while China should take the\par interim steps needed to shift away from its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg. He said the\par U.S. and China are in "broad agreement" on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, and that he\par expects the Chinese leadership to take further steps to ease capital\par controls and open the economy there.\par    -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 202 862 9249;\par elizabeth.price@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030911dz9b009vm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
