\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar drifts higher without much conviction.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases  \par \uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2003\par 16:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds Duisenberg and analyst comments, changes byline, changes dateline, previously LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted higher on Wednesday but without much conviction in the move as doubts linger over the pace of the U.S. economic recovery, leaving the greenback near three-week lows versus the euro and sterling.  \par \par \uc2 Persistent concerns in the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the dollar from falling in value against the yen, left it steady to slightly higher on the day.  \par \par \uc2 Doubts about the U.S. economic recovery were highlighted last week by a surprisingly weak U.S. jobs report that dovetailed with talk from Federal Reserve officials that U.S. benchmark interest rates are likely to remain at 1 percent, a 45 year low.  \par \par \uc2 These factors have muted optimism that the dollar would benefit from higher economic growth rates combined with an increase in jobs. More jobs aid consumer confidence and spending and increase tax revenue. Jobs, a lagging economic indicator have yet to contribute to rising gross domestic product.  \par \par \uc2 "Investors are still absorbing the idea that the Fed will stay on hold a bit longer than had been expected," said David Durrant, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank Julius Baer in New York, adding: "There is a tiny bit of a search for yield," driving interest away from the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In contrast, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said on Wednesday that euro zone interest rates are appropriate at 2 percent - indicating no cuts are expected in the foreseeable future - while inflation is on target, also at 2 percent, making the euro slightly more attractive.  \par \par \uc2 "Indications of an upturn in economic activity starting in the second half of the year have strengthened," Duisenberg told a the Economic and Monetary Affairs Committee in his last report before retiring at the end of October.  \par \par \uc2 Mike King, trader at Commerzbank in New York noted that Duisenberg's comments on growth prospects "had absolutely no effect on the market."  \par \par \uc2 Since last week, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shed almost 5 cents on the euro, retracing a substantial part of a rally that took it from record lows on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $1.1932 in June to a four-month peak of $1.0760 earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell to $1.1199 , off 0.24 percent, dropping from $1.1236 the previous session's three-week low of $1.1240.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the market is also mulling the longer-term impact of the rising U.S. budget deficit, which after U.S. President George W. Bush on Sunday asked Congress for an additional $87 billion, means it will exceed $500 billion.  \par \par \uc2 In Sweden, which holds a referendum on Sunday on whether to join Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the crown fell to a two-week low against the strengthening euro as opinion polls showed euro opponents increased their lead over euro supporters.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling traded at $1.5905 , off a bit for the day.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN HOLDS DOLLAR AT BAY  \par \par \uc2 Despite the economic doubts, the dollar found support against the yen with traders suspicious of Bank of Japan dollar buying interest around 116.80-70 yen . In morning New York trade, the dollar was up to 117.05 yen , a gain of 0.22 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The persistent upward pressure on the yen, which has driven much of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort, was also boosted on Wednesday after data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  growing at its fastest pace in two and a half years in the second quarter at one percent.  \par \par \uc2 The number was revised from the preliminary 0.6 percent reading.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said this may have driven the BoJ, which acts on behalf of the finance ministry in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, to step into the market again to protect export competitiveness from the painful effect of a strong yen.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ is leaning against the wind but it is becoming a pretty strong head-wind at this point," said Durrant.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030910dz9a002tz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
