\par\par \b \uc2 Yen steady in Europe, market wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2003\par 09:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The yen steadied versus the dollar in European trade on Wednesday, slipping into a very tight trading range after Japanese authorities apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling yen for dollars in New York trade to prevent the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Bank of Japan, which acts on behalf of the finance ministry in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, placed dollar bids around 116.80 yen again in Asian trade following an upward revision to Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) growth in April-June.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading stuck within a 116.71-116.99 per dollar range on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was also hugging tight ranges against both the dollar and the yen, holding just below a three-week high of $1.1240 set on the greenback on Tuesday on renewed worries on the U.S. economy.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0640 GMT, the euro stood at $1.1223  and 131.09 yen          ,\par unchanged on the day.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The economic data release schedule was thin. Only the U.S. mortgage market index was set to be published by the Mortgage Bankers Association of America.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets were also eyeing European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim Duisenberg's final quarterly testimony before the European Parliament's Economic and Monetary Committee at 1300 GMT.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow was also due to testify on government-sponsored enterprises Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac before a congressional committee at 1400 GMT.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Snow's testimony could shed light on future portfolio flows into the United States - needed to finance the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currenct\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  account deficit and support the dollar - in terms of how they can be affected by new agency oversight regulations.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030910dz9a001k5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
