\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA MARKETS-Stocks slide as SARS news batters airlines.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Richard Baum  \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2003\par 08:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The apparent return of the deadly SARS virus shook Asian stock markets on Wednesday as airline shares tumbled, overshadowing fresh signs of a reviving Japanese economy.   \par \par \uc2  An upward revision to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gross domestic product growth figures triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yen from strengthening, traders said, leaving the dollar little changed.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese government bonds crept higher as stocks fell, while oil and gold prices hardly budged.   \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's Nikkei average fell 0.6 percent from Tuesday's 14-month high to close at 10,856.32. An MSCI index of shares elsewhere in the Asia-Pacific fell three-quarters of a percent from a three-year peak.   \par \par \uc2  Airline stocks, and the Hong Kong market in particular, were hard hit by confirmation a medical researcher in Singapore had tested positive for SARS, which ravaged Asian tourism earlier in the year.   \par \par \uc2  A fall in U.S. shares following a revenue warning from top mobile phone maker Nokia also undermined Asian shares.   \par \par \uc2  "SARS has affected sentiment, but the market was due for some profit taking," said Herbert Lau, research director at Celestial Asia Securities in Hong Kong, where the Hang Seng Index was two percent weaker at midday.   \par \par \uc2  FEARS FOR HK TOURISM   \par \par \uc2  Cathay Pacific Airways Ltd tumbled 4.2 percent on concerns there could be a new SARS outbreak ahead of China's national day holiday in October, when many mainlanders are expected to visit Hong Kong.   \par \par \uc2  Shanghai-based China Eastern Airlines Corp Ltd shed six percent and its larger rival China Southern Airlines Co Ltd tumbled almost five percent.   \par \par \uc2  Japan Airlines System and Eva Airways also slumped, but Singapore Airlines was flat after falling six percent on Tuesday. The Singapore dollar also firmed on confidence the SARS case was an isolated one. The World Health Organisation said the case did not meet its definition of the disease.   \par \par \uc2  Benchmark indices fell 1.25 percent in Singapore, 0.6 percent in Australia and one percent in Taiwan South Korea was closed for a holiday.   \par \par \uc2  Shares in China, where SARS originated, held steady as investors snapped up stocks in drug companies likely to benefit from worries over the disease.   \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, industrial robot maker Fanuc Ltd and Ricoh Co Ltd, Japan's second-largest office machine maker, fell almost four percent after the Nokia warning helped wipe 0.8 percent off the U.S. Nasdaq index.   \par \par \uc2  But big banks jumped after revised data on Japan's GDP for April to June showed a rise of a real 1.0 percent from the previous quarter, up from an initial estimate of 0.6 percent growth.   \par \par \uc2  Mizuho Financial Group jumped 8.8 percent and UFJ Holdings gained 6.3 percent.   \par \par \uc2  "Banks should continue to rise steadily," said Hideki Kamiya, senior fund manager at Resona Asset Management. "They have passed the worst stage and while one needs to keep a cautious eye on the sector, banks are easy to buy when the market is in a bull run."   \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yen from strengthening after the GDP data, keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a tight range.   \par \par \uc2  At 0600 GMT, the dollar was trading around 118.88 yen almost flat from late U.S. trade. The dollar was also steady against the euro at $1.1220 retaining losses incurred on Tuesday on doubts over the sustainability of the U.S. economic rebound.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030910dz9a0008w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
