\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options:Japan Rumors Help Keeps Lid On Dlr/Yen Vols \b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2003\par 19:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Volatilities implied by one-month dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options moved slightly lower in New York Wednesday as reports of ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push the dollar up against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise above Y117 - moving further away from the psychologically important Y115 area - and relatively smooth trading after the huge swings Tuesday is pushing volatilities lower. \par \par \uc2  "It's very, very quiet today," said the senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Japanese bank in New York. "People are trying to reduce their risk exposure to dollar/yen...so there's less demand for hedge." \par \par \uc2  Around 1 p.m. EDT (1700 GMT), in the over-the-counter market, one-month at the money, or ATM, dollar/yen options implied volatility of 8.2%/8.5%, marginally lower than 8.25%/8.55% earlier Wednesday in Tokyo, and down from 8.50%/8.80% in New York Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders say the Bank of Japan, via agent banks, has been active the entire session buying dollars - as much as $4 billion - for yen. This has helped push the dollar as high Y117.24. Tuesday, it had sunk to Y116.10 before a round of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced it up to just below Y117.00. \par \par \uc2  But despite this, the market is still betting on the yen to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  "There's a strong interest for yen calls," the Japanese bank dealer said, noting that the dollar put/yen call bias on one-month quarter delta risk-reversals of around 1.0%/1.3%, against 1.0%/1.2% in Tokyo earlier Wednesday and 1.1%/1.4% in New York Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He also noted good demand for dollar/yen options at around Y107 and Y108 on a three- and five-month basis. \par \par \uc2  At 1 p.m. EDT (1700 GMT), the dollar was at Y117.19, just below the session high of Y117.24. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, volatilities implied by one-month ATM euro/yen options were slightly higher at 11.20%/11.45% compared with 11.00%/11.40% overnight in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Volatilities implied by one-month ATM euro/dollar options were slightly higher at 10.80%/11.00% from 10.70%/11.00% overnight in Tokyo, and 10.60%/11.00% in New York Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was weaker at $1.1184, coming off its three-week highs Tuesday of $1.1241, which is helping support volatilities Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Jamie McGeever, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 44427 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030910dz9a0015a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
