\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen buoyant on Nikkei, blocked by wariness on BOJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano  \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2003\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 9 (Reuters) - The yen stayed in a narrow band against the dollar on Tuesday as optimism over a rise in Tokyo share prices was countered by caution that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sap further gains in it.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say Japanese authorities could step in at any time to curb the export-damaging rise in the yen, given that its current level is slightly higher than early on Monday, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The Japanese government will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So the dollar will stay in a range between 115 and 118.50 yen for a while," said Kota Kimura, an assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 By 0524 GMT the dollar had eased to 116.55/60 yen compared with a late Monday New York level of 116.65/75 yen, with the greenback's rise to 117.72 yen in the aftermath of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday having evaporated.  \par \par \uc2 The yen remained well-bid because of renewed hope for Japanese shares.  \par \par \uc2 The stock market's key Nikkei average surged nearly two percent to an intraday high for the year after Morgan Stanley raised its recommended exposure to Japanese stocks to "overweight" from "neutral".  \par \par \uc2 "There is growing interest from foreigners in buying Japanese stocks and that is keeping the yen buoyant," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the corporate desk at Trust and Custody Services Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese machinery orders data for July came in slightly weaker than expected, but that failed to chase away yen bulls, with the yen continuing its recent uptrend, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Core private-sector machinery orders, a key gauge of trends in capital spending, fell 3.1 percent in July from a month earlier on a seasonally adjusted basis.  \par \par \uc2 That compared with a median forecast for a fall of 1.4 percent in a Reuters poll of 23 economists last week.  \par \par \uc2 SOFTENING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?  \par \par \uc2 Some traders tossed around the idea that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be urged to pull back from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers' meeting in Dubai later this month, amid criticism that Japan is in effect subsidising its exporters by trying to cheapen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But most market players think Japan will persist in curbing the yen's rise given its fragile economy after a decade-old slump, especially as long as China keeps its yuan pegged at current levels against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan is unlikely to compromise while China doesn't budge," said a fund manager at a European financial institution. "There may be some talk about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Dubai, but I don't expect anything more than at the last APEC meeting (in Thailand earlier this month)."  \par \par \uc2 The euro firmed slightly to $1.1099/04 against late Monday's U.S. level of $1.1066/72.  \par \par \uc2 The common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained some strength as market participants were careful about going overly long on the greenback amid nervousness ahead of the second anniversary of the September 11 attacks.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at 129.41/46 yen versus 129.25/36 yen in late U.S. trade.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was hampered by concerns that the euro zone's economic recovery may lag behind those in the United States and Japan.  \par \par \uc2 Still, such worries were offset by doubts about the U.S. recovery after surprisingly weak U.S. payrolls data on Friday and nervousness ahead of the September 11 anniversary.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030909dz99001ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
