\par\par \b \uc2 Yen curbed by BOJ wariness despite rising Nikkei.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano  \par \uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2003\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 9 (Reuters) - The yen was stuck in a narrow band versus the dollar on Tuesday as optimism over a rise in Tokyo share prices was countered by caution that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sap further gains in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Traders say that Japan could step in any time to curb the export-damaging rise in the yen, given the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current level is slightly higher than levels hit early on Monday when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese government will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So the dollar will stay in a range between 115 and 118.50 yen for a while," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 116.68/73 yen at 0255 GMT, almost flat from the late New York level, although the greenback's rise to 117.72 yen in the aftermath of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday had evaporated.   \par \par \uc2  The yen remained well-bid because of renewed hope for Japanese shares.   \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei average jumped more than 1.7 percent on Tuesday morning, hitting this year's intraday high after Morgan Stanley raised its recommended exposure to Japanese stocks to "overweight" from "neutral".   \par \par \uc2  "There is growing interest from foreigners in buying Japanese stocks and that is keeping the yen buoyant," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the corporate desk at Trust and Custody Services Bank.   \par \par \uc2  Sentiment may improve further if figures for Japan's machinery orders in July, due at 0500 GMT, come as a positive surprise. The median forecast by 23 economists polled by Reuters last week was for a fall of 1.4 percent.   \par \par \uc2  SOFTENING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?   \par \par \uc2  Some traders tossed around the idea that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be urged to pull back from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers' meeting in Dubai later in the month, amid criticism that Japan is in effect subsidising its exporters by trying to cheapen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But most market players think Japan will persist in curbing the yen's rise given its fragile economy after a decade-old slump, especially as long as China keeps its yuan pegged at current levels.   \par \par \uc2  "Japan is unlikely to compromise while China doesn't budge," said a fund manager at a European financial institution. "There might be some talk about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Dubai, but I don't expect anything more than the last APEC meeting (in Thailand earlier this month),"   \par \par \uc2  The euro firmed slightly to $1.1082/87 against Monday's late U.S. level of $1.1066/72, but it also moved in a narrow range.   \par \par \uc2  The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 129.27/39 yen versus 129.25/36 yen in late U.S. trade. The euro was hampered by concerns that the euro zone's economic recovery may lag behind recoveries in the United States and Japan.   \par \par \uc2  Still, such worries were offset by doubts about the U.S. recovery after surprisingly weak U.S. payroll data on Friday and nervousness ahead of the second anniversary of the September 11 attacks.   \par \par \uc2 Do