\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar climbs vs most rivals on equities rally.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2003\par 22:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against most major rivals on Monday in fairly sluggish trading as investors took direction from bullish equities in the absence of market-moving economic news.  \par \par \uc2 But the greenback failed to sustain a two-week high against the yen hit after Japanese authorities were cited once again selling their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was down 0.03 percent against the yen at 116.72 yen. The euro likewise fell 0.39 percent against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trading at 129.34 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against major European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. unit advanced, buoyed by gains in the stock market on upbeat reports from Wall Street analysts suggesting an economic rebound in the United States is on the way.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was changing hands at $1.1068 versus the dollar, down 0.34 percent. The dollar climbed 0.67 percent against the Swiss franc to 1.3908 francs. Sterling was also trading lower against the dollar at $1.5824, down 0.37 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 "It has been a slow trading day, although the market's focus right now is on the dollar-yen," said Kenneth Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Landon said it is perfectly clear that the Japanese government is determined to maintain its weak yen policy despite protests from the United States and Europe. "Investors should be careful about betting against the MoF (Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) at this time," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Trading sources said it appeared Japanese authorities sold yen to buy between $2 billion and $4 billion worth of dollars. Japan would not confirm its presence in the market.  \par \par \uc2 According to Enrico Caruso, chief dealer at Tempest Asset Management, some Japanese names are prepared to support the dollar against the yen at the 116.40 yen level and below.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot of players in the market are sort of focusing on 116.0 yen as the line in the sand support for the dollar," said Caruso.  \par \par \uc2 SPECULATOR BET  \par \par \uc2 Analysts also noted Friday's data showing speculators made the biggest bet in four years that the dollar would fall against the yen as a possible reason for Japan to step into the market with yen selling last week - and on Monday as well.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market intermittently since the middle of last week after its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose sharply on news Tokyo had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all in August.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Toshihiko Fukui declined to comment on the yen on Monday when he was questioned by reporters as he arrived at the G10 central bankers' meeting.  \par \par \uc2 The euro, meanwhile, traded somewhat weaker against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Landon of Deutsche Bank said investors tried to chase the euro higher against the dollar but failed to do so in the midst of a robust rally in the U.S. stock market.  \par \par \uc2 While relative growth fundamentals still favor the dollar in the medium term, analysts say the temporary dent to economic sentiment in the United States after a dismal labor report on Friday and the shift in the short-term technical bias suggests further euro gains against the dollar. (Additional reporting by Daniel Bases).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030908dz98003my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
