\par\par \b \uc2 Yen slips on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk, seen resilient.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shinichi Kishima  \par \uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2003\par 05:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The yen retreated against the dollar on Monday amid persistent talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities to halt a recent rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so as to keep Japan's export-led economic recovery on track.  \par \par \uc2 Still, no official confirmation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was available and the yen recovered some of its earlier losses in the absence of any further evidence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tweaking.  \par \par \uc2 Despite government efforts to muzzle the yen's rise, analysts said several factors would support yen strength in the near term: a strong stock market, improving economic data and the widely expected reelection of Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi as the leader of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party later in the month.  \par \par \uc2 Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at the Royal Bank of Scotland, said the yen would stay strong for the next few weeks, though its rise would be limited.  \par \par \uc2 "If the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is unchanged, it should stay around 115-120 (to the dollar)," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "(But) October is a new month. Koizumi should be reelected, and it will be the beginning of the second half of the fiscal year. In this circumstance we can have a little more yen appreciation."  \par \par \uc2 Although the dollar broadly fell on Friday after a weaker-than-expected U.S. jobs report, economists said the yen's level against the dollar would mainly rest on the degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market intermittently since the middle of last week after its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose sharply on news that Tokyo had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all in August.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's latest drop took place around 6:30 a.m. in Tokyo (2130 GMT, Sunday), and dealers said it was unusual for the authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at such hours, particularly on a Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The yen fell towards 117.75 to the dollar compared with 116.80 late in New York trade on Friday and 3-1/2-month highs around 115.75 set last week. But by 0300 GMT, it had clawed back up to around 117.30.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also fell beyond 130 to the euro for the first time in more than two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was steady against the dollar at around $1.11 holding on to gains it had made on Friday on the weak U.S. jobs data. U.S non-farm payrolls fell 93,000 versus forecasts for a 12,000 rise.  \par \par \uc2 YEN SEEN RESILIENT  \par \par \uc2 Traders said capital flows were likely to favour a stronger yen in the near term, with the Nikkei outperforming most of its main rival indices abroad and a recent volatility in the bond market making Japanese investors wary of buying foreign bonds.  \par \par \uc2 "If it were not for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - or all the talk about it - supply and demand in the market points towards lower dollar/yen levels," said a dealer at a Japanese trust bank.  \par \par \uc2 Figures for revised Japanese gross domestic product, due out on Wednesday, are expected to show the economy grew in April-June at a much faster pace than the government's original estimate of 0.6 percent from the previous quarter.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan figures showing a marginal increase in Japan's money supply and continued decline in bank lending had negligible effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Japan's most widely watched measure of money supply - M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) - rose 2.0 percent in August from a year earlier, compared with a rise of 1.8 percent in July.  \par \par \uc2 Lending by Japan's main banks fell 5.2 percent in August, the 68th consecutive month of decline.  \par \par \uc2 The economic data calendar for Monday was relatively light. But the market was expected to keep a close eye on any remarks from the Group of 10 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs' meeting in Basel.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030908dz98000gq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
