\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Weakens Against Euro, Pound on U.S. Jobless Data \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jamie McGeever \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 22:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -- The dollar's recent runup against its European rivals reversed in dramatic fashion Friday, as dealers sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily after a surprisingly weak U.S. employment report raised questions on the sustainability of the country's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The euro and sterling surged to two-week highs against the dollar on the news U.S. companies shed 93,000 jobs in August. Economists had expected an increase of 12,000. \par \par \uc2  The euro got an extra boost from strong buying by Japanese banks against the yen, which traders say was on behalf of the Bank of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped support the otherwise beleaguered dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Overall, however, it was a bad day for the greenback, which not even the second-consecutive monthly decline in the unemployment rate -- to 6.1% from 6.2% -- could disguise. It was a bad day for U.S. assets in general, apart from bonds, as the Dow Jones Industrials Average fell 0.9% and the Nasdaq Composite Index lost 0.6%. Yields on the 10-year Treasury plunged 0.17 percentage point on the day to 4.342%. \par \par \uc2  "The August employment report was a big disappointment," said Michael Woolfolk, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York. "Given that much of the dollar's rally this week was driven by speculative accounts fed by positive sentiment rather than real money trade and investment flows, it is not surprising that the dollar was set up for a fall despite [Japanese] \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  In late trading in New York Friday, the euro was at $1.1107, up from $1.0945 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was virtually unchanged at 116.83 yen, caught between the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday and heavy broad-based selling against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Sterling strengthened to $1.5900 from $1.5812. \par \par \uc2  The heavy selling sparked by the labor-market data sent the dollar crashing through several technical-support levels, which certainly muddy the dollar's near-term prospects. \par \par \uc2  Citibank, one of the largest market participants and dollar bulls, recommended Friday shifting to "neutral" dollar exposure against the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But other dollar bulls maintained confidence in its recovery powers. \par \par \uc2  Lauren Germain, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America in New York, said Friday's selling "was probably an overreaction to what is essentially a lagging indicator." \par \par \uc2  "We still see dollar strength," she added. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the issue of exchange-rate regimes remained in the spotlight Friday, even as U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow rounded off his week-long visit to Asia at a  meeting of Asian and Pacific Rim finance ministers in Thailand. \par \par \uc2  He told reporters a discussion on the merits of flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  systems will be high on the agenda when finance ministers from the Group of Seven industrialized nations meet in Dubai later this month. "It is a matter of principle and policy," said Mr. Snow. \par \par \uc2  He added the G-7 should set an example for developing economies, saying the group "ought to be using their voice to articulate the right framework for the conduct of the world trade system. Certainly the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  arrangements are one element for the framework of the global trading system." \par \par \uc2  North of the U.S. border, Canada also released weaker-than-expected jobs data, with the unemployment rate rising to a seasonally adjusted 8% in August from 7.8% in July. Employment fell by 19,000 in the month. But the Canadian dollar ended the day stronger against the dollar, which was trading at C$1.3698, versus C$1.3723 late Thursday. Earlier in the session, the U.S. dollar hit a two-month low of C$1.3654. \par \par \uc2  -By Jamie McGeever; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  09-05-03 1637ET \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020030905dz950040h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
