\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Finds Continued Support Vs Yen From BOJ \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miyako Takebe \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 07:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar remained firmly supported against the yen in Asia Friday, with few players willing to question Tokyo's resolve to use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb an excessive rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dollar bears were kept in line by the belief that Japan's finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were quietly slipping back into the market to buy dollars Friday, following up on their much more high-profile moves Thursday, when traders say the authorities spent about $5 billion buying dollars in Asian and other markets. \par \par \uc2  "There's been some unnatural movements near Y116.70 today, which leads us to believe that you-know-who is at it again," said a senior trader at a Japanese brokerage. \par \par \uc2  Market players believe the MOF will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as it's intent on keeping a strong yen from snuffing out the budding signs of improvement in Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Jonn Snow Friday repeated his view that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be kept to a minimum, but there was little market reaction to the remark "as it was aimed at China, not Japan," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HSBC in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. understands Japan has to keep the recovery intact. In that sense, the finance ministry's not the enemy," Ogino said. \par \par \uc2  The euro's strength against the yen was also regarded as another sign of Japanese authorities' presence in the market Friday, traders said, as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained the Y128 level despite little justification for the rise. \par \par \uc2  "It's not quite clear why the euro should rise so much right now. But at least it'll make a lot of Japanese institutional investors and exporters happy as they were likely left behind when the euro plunged earlier this week," said Minoru Shioiri, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Mitsubishi Securities. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.83, above Y116.73 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y116.81 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0961, higher than $1.0944 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.0838 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y128.05, up from Y127.75 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y126.88 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5857, up from $1.5812 in New York and higher than $1.5698 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely succeed for now in keeping the dollar up, many players are growing wary over how long Tokyo can maintain its current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, and how long Washington will continue to tolerate it. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar came under slight pressure Friday after a Reuters interview quoted Canadian Finance Minister John Manley as saying Snow will likely bring up \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Dubai meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers later this month. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, signs of improvement in Japan's economy and rising Tokyo share prices have led to an increase in capital inflows, putting upward pressure on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some traders say that while \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF may not stop \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely, it may have to gradually adjust its tactics to cope with shifting economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "It's probably better not to think that MOF is going to defend Y115 at all costs forever," Mitsubishi's Shioiri said. \par \par \uc2  In Phuket, Thailand, Asia-Pacific finance ministers Friday compromised on a post-meeting statement in terms of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, stopping short of endorsing a U.S. view that a flexible exchange rate is the best way to ensure economic growth and financial stability. \par \par \uc2  In a joint statement, finance ministers from the 21-member Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation forum called for "appropriate exchange rate policies," while merely noting the U.S. position. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated\par hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Doku