\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar rises vs yen, as traders cite Japan buying.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry and Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 19:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 5 (Reuters) - The dollar rebounded above the 117.0 yen mark against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday even as the greenback slumped against many other rivals, leading some New York-based traders to suspect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  or proxies had been actively engaged in yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official in New York declined to comment when asked whether the BoJ, acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had bought dollars for yen on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 When \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  occur, the BoJ acts on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders consulted had not seen actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but said they heard that Japanese commercial banks had sold yen against both the dollar and the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "I have not witnessed it, but the price action ... and the underlying bid tone to dollar/yen suggests that Tokyo banks continue to support both those \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs (the dollar against the yen and the euro against the yen)," said Scott Schultz, a trader with Brown Brothers Harriman in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar came under acute pressure against the euro and the Swiss franc, falling more than 1 percent against both as traders digested a weaker than expected U.S. August employment report released early in the North American session.  \par \par \uc2 Yet around midday in New York, the greenback went in the opposite direction against the yen , rising above the 117.0 yen mark for a gain of roughly 0.3 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 At about the same time, the push of the euro higher against the yen , snapping higher from 128.70 yen to way above the 129.0 yen area, was driven by Japanese accounts selling yen against the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Schultz said.  \par \par \uc2 "I think that was Japanese banks; that's what I am hearing ... I have not witnessed it," Schultz said.  \par \par \uc2 "We've heard of Japanese names, not sure if it's on behalf of the BoJ (Bank of Japan), bidding (for dollars) at 116.75 yen," said Hugh Walsh, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Fortis Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "People are just selling yen across the board because they believe that the BoJ will step in the dollar/yen (to buy dollars for yen) at 115.50 yen. We also heard that there were some big buyers of euros from Saudi Arabia," Walsh said.  \par \par \uc2 The 115.50 yen area and, below that, the 115.00 yen mark, have often been cited as key support levels for the dollar against the yen because traders see them as a de facto "line in the sand" below which Japan's government would be highly likely to step in, in order to curb yen strength.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's government is concerned with checking the appreciation of the yen in order to protect the competitiveness of Japanese exporters and nurture signs of a tentative recovery in the world's second biggest economy.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, traders suspected BoJ yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at levels well above the 115.50 mark. Then, Japanese officials did not confirm whether Japan had stepped in to buy dollars for yen.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, traders had the impression that bids for dollars by Japanese commercial banks, and perhaps by the BoJ itself, started to kick in when the dollar hit session lows around 116.42 yen on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030905dz95004r7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
