\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar rangebound vs yen on Snow, BOJ caution.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada  \par \uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was trapped in a tight range versus the yen on Friday as players shied away from testing Japan's commitment to stem the yen's rise, a day after Tokyo was seen aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.  \par \par \uc2 The yen got a lift from a series of warnings by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow against governments' heavy involvement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but gains were capped as dealers bet Japan could well step in should the dollar fall further.  \par \par \uc2 Some said there were vague rumours that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was passively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 116.70/80 yen.  \par \par \uc2 As of 0526 GMT, the greenback was trading at 116.84/87 yen, steady from late U.S. levels.  \par \par \uc2 "Yesterday's likely action was a strong sign that Japan is committed to protecting 115 yen," said Katsunori Kitakura, treasury manager at Chuo Mitsui Trust and Banking.  \par \par \uc2 The market expects a fall below that level, which Tokyo has successfully protected for over two years, would trigger options-related selling and slam the dollar to around 110 yen.  \par \par \uc2 But with Tokyo stock prices on a bull run on hopes for a much-awaited economic recovery and after calls from Washington for minimum \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts see a yen rise as inevitable.  \par \par \uc2 "Personally, I think 115 yen could be broken," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at JP Morgan Chase.  \par \par \uc2 SNOW URGES HANDS-OFF  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Treasury's Snow reaffirmed on Friday his belief that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be kept to a minimum.  \par \par \uc2 "We continually turn back to the idea that nobody can really devalue their way to prosperity," Snow told a news conference following a meeting of Asia-Pacific finance ministers in the Thai resort of Phuket.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier, Canadian Finance Minister John Manley, also in Thailand for the meeting, said Snow would be keen to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Group of Seven meets in Dubai later this month.  \par \par \uc2 As expected, the Asia-Pacific ministers, in their final communique, gave the nod to both sides of the argument over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be driven by market forces.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials, meanwhile, have not confirmed whether Japan stepped in to buy dollars for yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on whether the Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, saying only that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 The euro kept an upbeat tone versus the dollar and the yen ahead of U.S. jobs data at 1230 GMT, although it retreated modestly after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as expected, held its minimum bid rate at two percent.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts reckon U.S. unemployment stayed at 6.2 percent in August and non-farm payrolls increased by 12,000 compared with July's loss of 44,000, a Reuters poll showed.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.0965/70 versus $1.0939/45 in late New York trade. It was fetching 128.13/20 yen versus 127.69/85 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The market showed limited reaction to data on Friday showing a rise in Japan's diffusion index of leading economic indicators and a fall in overall household spending, both in July.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030905dz95000mu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
