\par\par \b \uc2 Canada says U.S. to discuss BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  at G7.  \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 PHUKET, Thailand, Sept 5 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow will be keen to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to hold down the yen when the Group of Seven meets in Dubai later this month, Canadian Finance Minister John Manley said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers reported determined \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to prevent the yen from approaching the key level of 115 to the dollar. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already spent nearly $80 billion this year, a record, to brake the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 Asked in a Reuters interview about the G7's attitude to Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Manley said, "It's going to be an issue that Mr Snow particularly is going to want to see pursued in that context."  \par \par \uc2 Snow, who, like Manley, is in Phuket for an Asia-Pacific finance ministers' meeting, visited Tokyo and Beijing on his way to Thailand.  \par \par \uc2 Manley said, "I think he'll want to talk about the Japanese. We know that one of the purposes of his trip to Japan was to include some discussion on that."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030905dz95000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
