\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Jumps A Yen On BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Bear Trap \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 990 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2003\par 07:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Goodbye Snow, hello \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Only days after the Tokyo visit of U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, a vocal critic of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market to buy dollars for yen during Asian trading, causing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shoot up more than a yen Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, buying dollars on orders from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pulled off a 'bear trap' - pushing up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate at a time when many players held short-dollar positions, prompting a massive wave of short-covering that propelled the dollar even higher, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after the dollar dropped on speculative selling to as low as Y115.75, a three-and-a-half month low and uncomfortably close in the minds of Japanese authorities to the psychologically key level of Y115.00. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities have repeatedly said they would act to prevent a strengthening in the yen that might take the wind out of Japan's economic recovery, and they were true to their words Thursday: the BOJ entered in force around Y115.75 to reverse the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, traders said. \par \par \uc2  More than ten major Japanese and U.S. banks were used in several rounds of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was thought to have bought at least $1 billion, traders said. The action moved the dollar to an intraday high of Y116.90. \par \par \uc2  "The MOF let the dollar decline and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was a bear trap," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows the ministry's strong resolve to keep the dollar above Y115.00, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities "do care about Y115," said Tomoko Fujii, a Nikko Citigroup strategist. "That was the line they tried to draw in May, and it looks like they're still sticking to that level." \par \par \uc2  One thing Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves no doubt about is that Japanese authorities are now back in the business of trying to guide the yen's exchange rate. Friday, the MOF surprised markets by revealing that it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all in August, after having sold Y9.07 trillion in the first seven months of the year. \par \par \uc2  Fujii said the MOF's apparent willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an obvious way, rather than covertly as it has done recently, suggests "they don't care about style - they just want to defend" the dollar against a fall toward Y115. \par \par \uc2  At 0430 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y116.81, above Y115.97 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y116.34 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at Y126.58, up from Y125.69 in New York late Wednesday. It was at Y125.52 in Tokyo late Wednesday. Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.0838, higher than $1.0836 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.0789 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5698, down from $1.5705 in New York, but higher than $1.5655 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials didn't immediately comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in line with their standard recent practice of not confirming or denying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  except by releasing official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data after the fact. But in the market, many players said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place. \par \par \uc2  One of the banks rumored to be executing yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  orders was a major Japanese bank recently accused of receiving a disproportionate share of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  orders, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  That could have been intentional, dealers added, as Japan's finance ministry may have been seeking to send a clear signal to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by using a bank widely known to act on the ministry's behalf. \par \par \uc2  Although the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tapered off in the afternoon, Tokyo is expected to continue to act as needed if the yen rises, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Y115 level is important in terms of technical charts because the dollar has stayed above that level since February 2001, with the help of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A three-point trendline support from a post Sept. 11 low of Y115.88 comes in Thursday at Y115.04, and technical analysts said a break below that level could pave the way for a move to Y110, or lower down, Y105. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities may actually prefer the dollar closer to Y117.88, said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities. \par \par \uc2  That is the average dollar/yen rate that large manufacturers predicted for the current fiscal year through March, according to the Bank of Japan's June tankan quarterly survey of business sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Washington is also likely to be tolerant of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ueno added. \par \par \uc2  "I think the U.S. is allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt (excessive) yen appreciation. Japan may have gotten understanding (from the U.S.) that Y115 is critical," he said. \par \par \uc2  Morgan Stanley's Umemoto agreed, saying the U.S. won't complain about the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least until general elections are held in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , probably toward the end of the year, as the U.S. wants Junichiro Koizumi to be re-elected as prime minister. Economic troubles caused by a rising yen could hurt Koizumi's re-election prospects. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, the dollar's sharp rise against the yen also boosted the euro more than Y1 to an intraday high of Y126.79 in the session. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030904dz940009x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pi