\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Japan Firms Boost Investment As Optimism Improves \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miyako Takebe \par \uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2003\par 06:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese firms boosted capital spending for the first time in almost two years in the April-June quarter, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey showed Thursday, providing more evidence that the world's second-largest economy is on a recovery path. \par \par \uc2  Higher corporate profits and rebounding share prices encouraged firms to boost capital investment by 6.4% in the three-month period from a year earlier, the first rise in seven quarters, the ministry said. \par \par \uc2  Economists say the robust survey results, which are used to calculate Japan's gross domestic product, are sure to bring about an upward revision to second-quarter GDP. Preliminary data for the quarter issued last month already shows stronger-than-expected annualized GDP growth of 2.3%. \par \par \uc2  "The surprising strength in capital spending suggests recent improvements in the corporate sector aren't just coming from restructuring efforts," said Mitsuru Saito, chief economist at UFJ Tsubasa Securities. "This will justify calls for a positive re-evaluation of Japan's economy." \par \par \uc2  Further good economic news came with the release of a separate MOF survey showing business sentiment improved in the July-September quarter. \par \par \uc2  The latest data follow a string of strong economic figures that has helped push up stock prices and interest rates and has fueled tentative expectations that Japan could emerge from its long deflationary slump. \par \par \uc2  But with the recovery far from assured, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday to stem a rise in the yen. A stronger yen could endanger export growth - still one of the key pillars for the Japanese economy despite better conditions domestically. \par \par \uc2  In a high-profile move, the Bank of Japan sold dollars for yen in Tokyo morning trading after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid below Y115.80, its lowest level since May 19. The dollar shot Y1 higher on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was quoted at Y116.83 at 0415 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Business Sentiment To Keep Improving\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the ministry's large company business sentiment index\par improved to -6.3 from -9.5 in the previous quarter, and is forecast to\par move back into positive territory in the October-December quarter with a\par reading of 2.6, which would show that more companies think economic\par conditions are good than bad. The index number hasn't been positive\par since the January-March period of 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The uncertainties hanging over the economy at the time of the\par previous survey, such as weak stocks, SARS and concerns over the U.S.\par economy, appear to be clearing," a MOF official said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo share prices have recently risen to 14-month highs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The brighter outlook in the latest survey is despite signs that\par unseasonably cool weather during the quarter has taken a toll on\par consumer spending.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Taken together, the surveys show that fundamentals and mood are\par coming into step with each other," UFJ's Saito said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Outside Japan too, economists are turning more optimistic - at least\par for the immediate future.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The World Bank on Wednesday raised its 2003 growth forecast for Japan\par to 0.8% from its April prediction of 0.6%. But it lowered its 2004\par forecast to 1.3% from 1.6%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In its Global Economic Prospects report, the bank noted Japan's recent\par recovery in the corporate sector, saying "profits of major manufacturers\par experienced a substantial comeback, rising 38% in recent quarters."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development also weighed\par into the debate, with its chief economist, Jean-Philippe Cotis, saying\par deflation is waning. Still, he said the Bank of Japan should maintain\par its easy policy "for a while" until "there are really tangible results\par visible."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Corporate Profits, Sales Also Up In 2Q\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In addition to rising capital spending, the MOF's business activity\par survey found corporate current profits rose 13.6% from a year earlier, a\par faster pace than the 10.0% increase in the previous quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Corporate sales rose 2.4% from a year ago after falling 1.4% in the\par previous quarter, the ministry also said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 6.4%-rise in overall corporate capital expenditure in the\par April-June quarter came on the back of a strong increase in such\par spending by non-manufacturers, which lifted their investment by 7.7%.\par Manufacturers increased capital spending by 3.8%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manufacturers continued to contribute most to the overall rise in\par profits, marking a gain of 36.3% in April-June, nearly unchanged from a\par 36.6% rise in the previous quarter. Non-manufacturers' profits rose\par 1.6%, compared with a 1.2% drop in January-March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manufacturers' sales rose 3.9% on year in April-June, up from the\par previous quarter's 3.6% gain, and those of non-manufacturers rose 1.8%,\par an improvement from January-March's 3.3% fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Ron Harui contributed to this report)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by John Gibson\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030904dz940008x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
