\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -BoJ pushes yen down, euro pays little heed to ECB.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2003\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 4 (Reuters) - The yen fell one percent from a 3-1/2 month high against the dollar on Thursday after Japan apparently sold it heavily, while the euro took little notice of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to hold rates steady.  \par \par \uc2 Japan gave no confirmation whether it had stepped in but Tokyo traders saw the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the finance ministry, selling yen and pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down more than one yen.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the ECB kept interest rates at a record low of two percent, in line with expectations, as the euro zone economy showed signs of modest economic rebound. The Bank of England also held rates unchanged at 3.5 percent, a 48-year low.  \par \par \uc2 The ECB was due to hold a news conference, headed by deputy chief Lucas Papademos, at 1230 GMT. ECB President Wim Duisenberg was not at the rate meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Investors will be paying close attention to the ECB's tone for hints whether the region's economy may still need another push from a rate cut.  \par \par \uc2 "This is very much expected and thus giving no impact to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Eventually, however, the ECB will lower rates because of the euro zone's overall economic performance," said David Mann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in London.  \par \par \uc2 "By contrast, the Japanese economy is doing much better than many people had expected. But (they are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  because) they still want to make sure the recovery is on track and they are keen not to lose competitiveness," he said.  \par \par \uc2 By 1300 GMT, the yen was trading above the day's low of 116.98 but it was still nearly one percent down from late New York. Against the euro it fell about 1.5 yen from the day's high to 126.43 after hitting a 7-1/2 month peak beyond 125 yen on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was down 0.23 percent on the day versus the dollar at $1.0818, off Wednesday's four-month low. It ticked lower once the ECB rate decision was out of the way.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN STRIKES BACK  \par \par \uc2 The yen action came as market speculation grew Japan may become less aggressive in holding the yen down due either to domestic economic recovery or pressure from Washington not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively.  \par \par \uc2 Such pressure was reinforced by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow in a visit this week.  \par \par \uc2 Also a Japanese finance ministry survey showed Japanese companies boosted spending on plant and equipment by 6.4 percent in the April-June quarter from the same period a year earlier, the first rise in seven quarters.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts said the Japanese government, which spent a record nine trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first seven months of this year, is determined to block the yen's rise, fearing it could derail the economy by hurting exporters. "Price action clearly shows there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The message \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sending is its broad strategy of preventing a freefall in dollar/yen remains unchanged, despite Snow's visit," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC MENACE?  \par \par \uc2 ECB policymakers have sent a clear message recently that with money cheap and plentiful in a slowly recovering economy, they intend to leave interest rates unchanged on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Council member Ernst Welteke, in an interview published by Britain's Daily Mail, questioned what lower interest rates would achieve for the 12-nation euro zone.  \par \par \uc2 But even though recent economic data for the euro zone provided grounds for cautious optimism, much still depends on a global recovery, powered by the United States, that could in turn revitalise Europe's growth, economists said.  \par \par \uc2 Five officials from the Federal Reserve give speeches in separate events due later in New York trading hours.  \par \par \uc2 And markets are also eyeing the U.S. ISM non-manufacturing survey for August due at 1400 GMT. The index is expected to fall to 63.0 from 65.1 in July.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030904dz94003ph\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs